# Ready-made API calls for manual testing.
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above a call.
# Start the server first (npm start). Run "Sign in" first: REST Client keeps the cookie.

@base = http://localhost:3000

### Health check (public)
GET {{base}}/api/health

### FR-01 Sign in with a wrong password → 401
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "anna@stelisabeth.de", "password": "wrong" }

### FR-01 Sign in → 200 and a session cookie
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "anna@stelisabeth.de", "password": "demo1234" }

### FR-01 Who is signed in?
GET {{base}}/api/auth/me

### FR-02 Dashboard KPIs, nearest expiry, latest requests
GET {{base}}/api/dashboard

### FR-03 Products: search, category and stock status filters
GET {{base}}/api/products?search=becor&category=Coronary stents&status=below

### FR-04 One product with lots and suggested quantity
GET {{base}}/api/products/2

### FR-04 Unknown product → 404
GET {{base}}/api/products/999

### FR-05 Mark lot 1 as "use first"
PATCH {{base}}/api/lots/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "useFirst": true }

### FR-10 Open removals
GET {{base}}/api/removals?status=open

### FR-07 Requests list, newest first (filters optional)
GET {{base}}/api/requests?status=Submitted&type=replenishment

### FR-07 One request
GET {{base}}/api/requests/3

### FR-06 Create a request → 201 (remember the new id for the next calls)
POST {{base}}/api/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "replenishment", "productId": 2, "quantity": 10, "reason": "", "notes": "For next week" }

### FR-06 Invalid request (quantity 0) → 400 with fields
POST {{base}}/api/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "usage", "productId": 2, "quantity": 0 }

### FR-08 Edit a Submitted request → 200 (change 3 to your new id if you like)
PUT {{base}}/api/requests/3
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "return", "productId": 7, "quantity": 2, "reason": "Overstock", "notes": "" }

### FR-08 Edit an Approved request → 409
PUT {{base}}/api/requests/2
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "usage", "productId": 1, "quantity": 2, "reason": "Used in procedure", "notes": "" }

### FR-09 Withdraw a Submitted request → 204
DELETE {{base}}/api/requests/3

### FR-09 Withdraw an Approved request → 409
DELETE {{base}}/api/requests/2

### FR-11 Explain an open removal → 200
PATCH {{base}}/api/removals/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Other", "note": "Moved to room 2 for an emergency" }

### FR-11 Explain the same removal again → 409
PATCH {{base}}/api/removals/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Damaged" }

### FR-01 Sign out → 204
POST {{base}}/api/auth/logout
